{"name":"Ancient Marble","hex":"#d1ccb9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ancient","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having lasted from a remote period; having been of long duration; of great age, very old.","Existent or occurring in time long past, usually in remote ages; belonging to or associated with antiquity; old, as opposed to modern."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is very old.","A person who lived in ancient times."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancient"},{"term":"marble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metamorphic rock of crystalline limestone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A small ball used in games, originally of marble but now usually of glass or ceramic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something to have) the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example by mixing viscous ingredients incompletely, or by applying paint or other colorants unevenly.","To get or have the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example due to the incomplete mixing of viscous ingredients, or the uneven application of paint or other colorants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ancient history","blocks":[{"text":"Ancient history is a time period from the beginning of writing and recorded human history through late antiquity. The span of recorded history is roughly 5,000 years, beginning with the development of Sumerian cuneiform script. Ancient history covers all continents inhabited by humans in the period 3000 BC – AD 500."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg/330px-Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_history"},{"title":"Marble","blocks":[{"text":"Marble is a metamorphic rock consisting of carbonate minerals (most commonly calcite (CaCO3) or dolomite (CaMg(CO3)2) that have recrystallized under the influence of heat and pressure. It has a crystalline texture, and is typically not foliated (layered), although there are exceptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Marmo_z17.JPG/330px-Marmo_z17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg/500px-CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg/1280px-CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg/500px-CairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACairoEgMuseumTaaMaskMostlyPhotographed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Mohenjo-daro_Priesterk%C3%B6nig.jpeg/500px-Mohenjo-daro_Priesterk%C3%B6nig.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Mohenjo-daro_Priesterk%C3%B6nig.jpeg/500px-Mohenjo-daro_Priesterk%C3%B6nig.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMohenjo-daro_Priesterk%C3%B6nig.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Front_views_of_the_Venus_de_Milo.jpg/500px-Front_views_of_the_Venus_de_Mi